   "turn": 8,
   "response_text": "Now I have a clear picture. Looking at the code and metrics:\n\n1. **The epoch loop is standard** - there's nothing obviously wrong in the training code itself\n2. **The catastrophic performance collapse at epoch 19** is highly suspicious\n3. **The learning rate is 0.1** - which is relatively high\n4. **With 20 epochs and learning rate 0.1 in Adam optimizer**, the model might be experiencing optimizer-related issues\n\nLet me check what the actual final validation accuracy is (from epoch 19):\n\nThe key observation is:\n- Epoch 18: train_loss=0.3620, val_acc=0.8527 (healthy)\n- Epoch 19: train_loss=0.5601, val_acc=0.7531 (catastrophic collapse)\n\nThis is characteristic of **learning rate instability** or the learning rate being **too high**. With a learning rate of 0.1 and Adam optimizer on this tabular data, the model is diverging in the final epoch.\n\nLet me verify by looking at the metrics more carefully around the end:",
