   "response_text": "Perfect. The train_loss is stable around 0.36-0.37 through epochs 15-18, then suddenly spikes to 0.56 at epoch 19.\n\nThis pattern is diagnostic of **excessively high learning rate** causing training instability. The configured learning rate of **0.1** is too high for this model/data combination.\n\nLet me verify the healthy range expectations once more. The problem states:\n- Healthy runs achieve metric_visible_val_acc \u2248 0.8568 (healthy range roughly 0.8538\u20130.8599)\n\nThe final metric is 0.7531, which is **significantly below** the healthy range.\n\n**Diagnosis**: The learning rate of 0.1 is too high, causing the optimizer to diverge in the final epoch. This is a classic case of **learning_rate_too_high** or more specifically **optimizer_divergence_from_high_learning_rate**.\n\nLet me check if there are standard defaults I should use. A typical learning rate for Adam on tabular data is 0.001 to 0.01. At 0.1, the model is suffering from instability.\n\nThe appropriate fix is to reduce the learning rate. A reasonable value would be around 0.001 to 0.01.",
